            <partial name="_SkillVfxChain" />
        </div>

        @* ── Archeon atlas ───────────────────────────────── *@
        <section id="atlas" class="sec-block" aria-labelledby="atlas-title">
            <header class="sec-head" data-reveal>
                <p class="kd-eyebrow">Case study · Worldbuilding</p>
                <h2 id="atlas-title" class="sec-title">Archeon world atlas</h2>
                <p class="sec-lede">An AI-assisted world-simulation pipeline for my SKBS universe. Terrain for the planet Archeon is built up stage by stage. Each stage keeps its candidates, its numbers and a note of what it does <em>not</em> yet prove.</p>
            </header>

            <ol class="sec-pipeline" aria-label="Pipeline stages" data-reveal>
                <li><span>Tectonics</span></li>
                <li><span>Erosion</span></li>
                <li><span>Climate</span></li>
                <li><span>Regional terrain</span></li>
            </ol>

            <div class="sec-cards">
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal>
                    <span class="sec-card-k">01 · Tectonics</span>
                    <h3>Uplift, faults, rifts</h3>
                    <p>Uplift, fault-block offsets and basalt cover on a ~16 km continental grid. One rift was rebuilt as an extensional valley about 1,500 km long, bounded by segmented normal faults.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <span class="sec-card-k">02 · Erosion</span>
                    <h3>Two million years, three seeds</h3>
                    <p>24 comparison runs — three seeds, four regions, two processes — over two million effective years. Weathering, river incision, deposition, hillslope transport and export to the sea are accounted separately.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
                    <span class="sec-card-k">03 · Climate <span class="kd-badge">IN PROGRESS</span></span>
                    <h3>Short control runs only</h3>
                    <p>So far: short control runs, and a radiative-transfer benchmark that reproduces its official reference values. These are not yet a global climate result, and the pages say so.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal>
                    <span class="sec-card-k">04 · Regional terrain <span class="kd-badge">REWORK</span></span>
                    <h3>Back to the drawing board</h3>
                    <p>The first close-up regions, a voxel terrain prototype for the Orun plateau and a terrace scene for Atheria, no longer match the current planet model. Both are off the public atlas; the voxel logic stays in the codebase for the next pass.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <span class="sec-card-k">Verification</span>
                    <h3>Hashes before claims</h3>
                    <p>Every atlas refresh is checked: SHA-256 for each imported asset, syntax checks, map dependency graphs and HTTP checks for every resource. When 3D behaviour wasn’t rechecked in a browser, the log says so.</p>
                </article>
            </div>

            <div class="kd-link-row" style="margin-top: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 28px);" data-reveal>
                <a class="kd-pill kd-pill-primary" href="/archeon-atlas/index.html">Open the atlas</a>
                <a class="kd-pill" href="/Archeon">Archeon story page</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        @* ── This site ───────────────────────────────────── *@
        <section id="site" class="sec-block" aria-labelledby="site-title">
            <header class="sec-head" data-reveal>
                <p class="kd-eyebrow">Case study · This website</p>
                <h2 id="site-title" class="sec-title">This site</h2>
                <p class="sec-lede">This version was rebuilt by directing AI agents in parallel — one on the global look and interactions, others on the content pages — then merged and checked in a browser.</p>
            </header>

            <div class="sec-cards">
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal>
                    <span class="sec-card-k">Split</span>
                    <h3>Strict file ownership</h3>
                    <p>Each agent owned a fixed set of files in the same checkout and left everything else alone, so parallel work never collided.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <span class="sec-card-k">Contract</span>
                    <h3>Components specified up front</h3>
                    <p>Scroll reveals, the lightbox, filter chips and placeholders were defined as markup first, so content pages could be written against them before they existed.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="sec-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
                    <span class="sec-card-k">Check</span>
                    <h3>Merged, then verified</h3>
                    <p>Every route checked for status and content, every image path checked on disk — then the merged result reviewed by eye, on desktop and on a phone-width screen.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</section>

